  "status": "Real V8 verifier defect reproduced and fix prepared. Native branch controls pass with the six exact reachable allocations approved. Full updated RPM and ARM qualification remain required.",
  "root_cause": "VerifyExternalStringResource leaves expected uninitialized when a string has an external forwarding index for a one-byte resource. GetExternalStringResourceSlow correctly returns nullptr for that input. The verifier then compares an indeterminate pointer with nullptr.",
  "baseline": "Unmodified candidate5 libnode24.18.1 ordinary external one-byte control passes; --shared-string-table internalized one-byte control aborts at expected == value. The check is exported in Release but called automatically only by checking builds; this test explicitly invokes the exported member ABI to avoid a V8_ENABLE_CHECKS initialization mismatch.",
  "fix": "Assign nullptr for a forwarded one-byte resource and the resource pointer for a two-byte resource. No compiler flag change, suppression or disabled verifier. Patch17 plus native Source21 regression prepared.",
  "native_branch_control": "The exact verifier method and corrected assignment compile with package feature/ABI flags. Its hidden forwarding-table lookup helper is adapted to the public GetExternalStringResourceBase getter, which queries the same real table. All other method operations and real V8 strings are unchanged. Original and fixed adapters reproduce the failure/pass pair. Direct linking of the unchanged helper fails because isolate globals are hidden; this adapter is diagnostic-only and is not shipped.",
